(1573206, 210691, 37234, '<td valign="top">Looks a bit too well dressed, IMO. Was expecting him to look more grungy. Like the walls, which are amazing. My pick for top 3.</td>', 'Looks a bit too well dressed, IMO. Was expecting him to look more grungy. Like the walls, which are amazing. My pick for top 3.', '2005-07-30 01:57:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1573207, 210916, 34247, '<td valign="top">I think this is a funny idea and a nice addition to the challenge on that level. When it comes to the execution, I find the lighting a bit fluorescent, and flat. I''d like to point out the possibility that the use of "photojihad" as a name might strike some people as insensitive and carries lots of religious connotation. I think you''d successfully made the point, even without the use of "jihad," a term that I think is very loaded these days. I''m not taking it personally, and I''m not trying to be PC. I just think some people might find "jihad" a disturbing and derogatory reference, and one that doesn''t necessarily add to the already high humor value of this image. 6</td>', 'I think this is a funny idea and a nice addition to the challenge on that level. When it comes to the execution, I find the lighting a bit fluorescent, and flat. I''d like to point out the possibility that the use of "photojihad" as a name might strike some people as insensitive and carries lots of religious connotation. I think you''d successfully made the point, even without the use of "jihad," a term that I think is very loaded these days. I''m not taking it personally, and I''m not trying to be PC. I just think some people might find "jihad" a disturbing and derogatory reference, and one that doesn''t necessarily add to the already high humor value of this image. 6', '2005-07-30 01:57:15.000000', NULL, 1),
