(1590884, 210874, 15497, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by beaflies:</b></div><hr/><i> Could you explain the lense you used?  Is the Aspherical DG to correct for warped appearances of wide-angle views?  Just beginning to learn about lenses and filters since I do not own an SLR - yet!<br/>Thank you and Congrats! this was one of my favorites<br/>-bea </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hey Bea,<br/> <br/>I used the Sigma 12-24mm f/4.5-5.6 EX lens, it''s taken at 12mm also.<br/>No filter was used. I have cropped a little bit, maybe about 3-5% of the photo. It''s important to remember that the 20D has a 1.6x crop, making the actual focal length 19,2mm. This surely helps on removing a lot of the "barrel" view it would give you on a fullframe or 1.3x crop body. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by beaflies: Could you explain the lense you used?  Is the Aspherical DG to correct for warped appearances of wide-angle views?  Just beginning to learn about lenses and filters since I do not own an SLR - yet!Thank you and Congrats! this was one of my favorites-bea   Hey Bea, I used the Sigma 12-24mm f/4.5-5.6 EX lens, it''s taken at 12mm also.No filter was used. I have cropped a little bit, maybe about 3-5% of the photo. It''s important to remember that the 20D has a 1.6x crop, making the actual focal length 19,2mm. This surely helps on removing a lot of the "barrel" view it would give you on a fullframe or 1.3x crop body. ', '2005-08-06 13:34:33.000000', NULL, 0),
