(1593240, 210710, 25397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pcody:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh man. The dreaded "new camera, I didn''t think to check the date problem." <br/>Actually, this was a devious plot some evil person (was it Dan) to keep you from winning all the time. The camera can pick out the really great shots(well, with you, which one isn''t) and imprint the wrong date on it. But the real spooky thing is, the exif data you look at will always be correct. It''s only when you have to send the full unedited version to the sc that the exif converts to the wrong date. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Part one of the exciting ''double DQ'' series! A uploading program messed my original EXIF and I didn''t keep the original on cam.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by pcody: Oh man. The dreaded "new camera, I didn''t think to check the date problem." Actually, this was a devious plot some evil person (was it Dan) to keep you from winning all the time. The camera can pick out the really great shots(well, with you, which one isn''t) and imprint the wrong date on it. But the real spooky thing is, the exif data you look at will always be correct. It''s only when you have to send the full unedited version to the sc that the exif converts to the wrong date.  Part one of the exciting ''double DQ'' series! A uploading program messed my original EXIF and I didn''t keep the original on cam.', '2005-08-08 00:28:25.000000', NULL, 0),
